think The granted ruling's own design (active-designing/20260825-173153) ranks its moves safety-first, and the reading came before the writing: Move 1 -- the content-keyed build receipt -- is already LANDED in rye/src/main.rye as ryekey-v2 with a fifteen-leg control, and it is ALIVE on this bench: the control ran CONTROL_GREEN here, six flips missed, the hit held, the bypass rebuilt, two fresh builds agreed. Measured on metal: the drain-replay witness runs 4.46 s on a cold build and 1.27 s on the receipt hit -- a 3.5x wall reduction, the compile fraction near 72 percent of that witness's time.
think One tension named rather than crossed: the caravan suite's cold-clear (REDS %92's own lesson) deletes caravan/bin with its receipts, so the choir rebuilds all 113 every sing -- the receipt's fifteen-leg control now proves staleness-impossibility better than deletion does, but relaxing a seated cold rule brushes the FAST/COLD law, so it is surfaced for Keaton beside the ruling he already holds.
think Move 2's engineering gate is a hit rate nobody had measured, so the runner grew the meter and nothing else: at every open it compares the tree digest against the last fully green close's receipt and prints roster_receipt=none|miss|match, appending one row per open to a rolling ledger; at a fully green unmoved close it writes the receipt. Both shelves are untracked beside the runs card, env-overridable for controls, and consulted by NOTHING that skips a guard -- the meter exists so the ruling can be made on a number instead of a mood. A --receipt-probe flag stops after the compare with its own verdict, runs zero guards, and never wears the roster's green.
obs Proven on metal in a pen: none, miss, and match legs each read true through the probe, and the ledger accreted one row per open. The runner's own control stands CONTROL_GREEN exit 0 over the edits. The write leg fires only in the real ok path, so its first proof is the next genuine green close -- named here rather than claimed.
obs The card's nib refreshes in this commit per the guard's own prescription (it rode one generation stale since the standfast seat, by design never by a pin-only follow-up).
